- `w ≥ e0+10` and `w+t < 2069`: the port is `w`. The cut keeps it at its stock value, and the stock state has
  the whole 257-wire carry `1556..1812` clean (`WideReference.full_carry` from `Domain`).
- `w+t ≥ 2069` (only `t = 375, 390`): the port is `q = 3113-w ∈ [1414, 1044+t]`. The cut keeps it at the stock
  value of `OB5.sig (t-1) q`. That is `w`, in the clean carry top, or for `q = 1044+t` the history cell of tick
  `t`, clean by `future_history`.
Enter, first tick and pack never touch these ports. -/

/-- Unwrapped upper ports (`w+t < 2069`) for `j ≤ 21`: untouched by the pack and the first tick. -/
theorem mid_support (j : Fin 23) (h21 : j.val≤21) {w : Nat} (lo : e0P (start j)+10≤w) (nw : w+start j<2069) :
